[Round 2/8 | Implementer | 53.7s | 0/400k] The current M2 structure is semantically close, but it pays two contended `std::sync::Mutex` acquisitions per successful enqueue/dequeue and the publication heap repeatedly dereferences `UnsafeCell` slot metadata during comparisons. I’m going to preserve the two-phase ownership protocol while tightening the hot path: use a lightweight short-held lock, keep publication keys in heap entries, and remove unnecessary tie-order metadata (ties are explicitly arbitrary).

